{"type":"Environment","id":"free_c9bc8b1e8ecd-ba0f1b544ad3","meta":{"status":"ready","error":null},"title":"Pendulum length and time for one swing","lane":"free","label":"model-checked","kitVersion":"0.1.0","htmlSha256":"ba0f1b544ad3c2630f554fb28bff592ca75648c07f8014f7141faa77130e03c7","html":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline' http://localhost:3001/vendor/; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; font-src http://localhost:3001/vendor/ data:; connect-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none';\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>Pendulum length and time for one swing</title><style>\n:root{--bg:#ffffff;--fg:#2f3a34;--muted:#4f5d57;--accent:#0a776b;--card:#f7f8f4;--border:#d3dace;--bench:#fbfcf8;--try:#8a3340;--step:#6b4aa0;--gold:#8f6100;--goldsoft:#fff8e6;--goldborder:#ecd9a6;color-scheme:light}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){:root:not([data-theme=\"light\"]){--bg:#16201c;--fg:#e9efea;--muted:#a4b2ab;--accent:#16b6a3;--card:#0e1512;--border:#34403a;--bench:#121a16;--try:#f0a3ad;--step:#b9a0e6;--gold:#e8b84a;--goldsoft:#2a2414;--goldborder:#5a4a1c;color-scheme:dark}}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]{--bg:#16201c;--fg:#e9efea;--muted:#a4b2ab;--accent:#16b6a3;--card:#0e1512;--border:#34403a;--bench:#121a16;--try:#f0a3ad;--step:#b9a0e6;--gold:#e8b84a;--goldsoft:#2a2414;--goldborder:#5a4a1c;color-scheme:dark}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}\nmain.lab{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px;display:grid;gap:14px}\n.kicker{margin:0;font:700 .75rem/1.2 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}\nh1{margin:.2rem 0 .3rem;font-size:1.6rem;line-height:1.2}\nh2{margin:0 0 .4rem;font-size:1rem;letter-spacing:.02em}\n.try{margin:0;padding:10px 14px;border-left:4px solid var(--try);background:var(--card);border-radius:10px}\n.try strong{color:var(--try)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:10px 16px}\n.idea{background:var(--goldsoft);border-color:var(--goldborder)}\n.idea h2{color:var(--gold)}\n.idea p{margin:.2rem 0}\n.top{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.steps ol{margin:0;padding-left:1.4rem}\n.steps li{padding-left:2px}\n.predict ul{margin:.2rem 0 .4rem;padding-left:1.2rem}\nsummary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;font-weight:600;color:var(--accent)}\n.benchrow{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.bench{background:var(--bench);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:8px;overflow:hidden}\n.bench svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:520px;touch-action:none}\n.side{display:grid;gap:12px;align-content:start}\n.readouts{display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(140px,1fr))}\n.readout{background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:8px 12px}\n.readout .name{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.readout output{display:block;font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.found{margin:0;border-color:var(--accent)}\n.found:empty{display:none}\n.fine summary{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,auto) 1fr;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px}\n.row label{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.row input[type=range]{width:100%;min-height:44px;accent-color:var(--accent)}\n.hints details{border-top:1px solid var(--border)}\n.hints details:first-of-type{border-top:0}\n.explain p{margin:.3rem 0}\n@media (min-width:760px){.top{grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr}.benchrow{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(260px,1fr)}}\n\n#bench-art .lbl { fill: var(--fg); font-size: 14px; font-family: inherit; }\n#bench-art .mut { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; font-family: inherit; }\n#bench-art .str { stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 2; }\n#bench-art .arc { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }\n#bench-art .guide { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }\n#bench-art .knobdot { fill: var(--accent); stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 2; }\n#bench-art .tk { stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 1.5; }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n  #bench-art .knobdot { transition: fill 0.2s; }\n}</style></head><body><main class=\"lab\"><header><p class=\"kicker\">Physics, Form 4</p><h1>Pendulum length and time for one swing</h1><p class=\"try\"><strong>Try this:</strong> Drag the round knob on the ruler up and down to change the length of the swinging pendulum.</p></header><div class=\"top\"><section class=\"card idea\"><h2>Key idea</h2><p>A longer pendulum takes longer for each swing. The time for one full swing (the period) depends on the length and on g, not on the mass of the bob.</p><p>T = 2 x pi x sqrt(L / g)</p></section><section class=\"card predict\"><h2>Predict first</h2><p>You make the pendulum 4 times longer, for example from 0.25 m to 1.00 m. What happens to the period T?</p><ul><li>T becomes 2 times longer</li><li>T becomes 4 times longer</li><li>T becomes 16 times longer</li></ul><details><summary>Check your prediction</summary><p>Drag the knob to 0.25 m and read T, then drag it to 1.00 m and read T again. Divide the second by the first.</p></details></section></div><section class=\"card steps\"><h2>Steps</h2><ol><li>Drag the knob to 0.25 m. Watch your pendulum swing together with the grey reference pendulum, which is also 0.25 m long. They swing in step.</li><li>Drag the knob down to 1.00 m. Watch your pendulum fall behind the reference and read the period T.</li><li>Drag the knob to 0.10 m, then to 0.40 m, then to 0.90 m. Compare the readouts for L, T and T squared.</li><li>Look at T squared each time you double L. See how T squared changes when L doubles.</li></ol></section><section class=\"benchrow\" aria-label=\"The lab bench\"><div class=\"bench\"><svg id=\"bench-art\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 440\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pendulum of length 0.50 metres beside a 0.25 metre reference pendulum\">\n<defs>\n<radialGradient id=\"bobg\" cx=\"35%\" cy=\"35%\" r=\"70%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#ffd27a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#c9772a\"/></radialGradient>\n<radialGradient id=\"refg\" cx=\"35%\" cy=\"35%\" r=\"70%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#e3e6ea\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#7d8794\"/></radialGradient>\n</defs>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"440\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"var(--bench)\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"36\" width=\"360\" height=\"14\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"var(--muted)\"/>\n<line class=\"tk\" x1=\"70\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"410\"/>\n<g id=\"ticks\"></g>\n<text class=\"lbl\" x=\"70\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Length L (m)</text>\n<text class=\"lbl\" x=\"270\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your pendulum</text>\n<text class=\"lbl\" x=\"500\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reference 0.25 m</text>\n<line id=\"guide\" class=\"guide\" x1=\"70\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"230\"/>\n<path id=\"arcM\" class=\"arc\" d=\"\"/>\n<path id=\"arcR\" class=\"arc\" d=\"\"/>\n<line id=\"strM\" class=\"str\" x1=\"270\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"230\"/>\n<circle id=\"bobM\" cx=\"270\" cy=\"230\" r=\"15\" fill=\"url(#bobg)\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<line id=\"strR\" class=\"str\" x1=\"500\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"140\"/>\n<circle id=\"bobR\" cx=\"500\" cy=\"140\" r=\"11\" fill=\"url(#refg)\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text id=\"tM\" class=\"lbl\" x=\"294\" y=\"78\">T = 1.42 s</text>\n<text id=\"tR\" class=\"mut\" x=\"524\" y=\"78\">T = 1.00 s</text>\n<g id=\"knob\" data-synapse-handle=\"length\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"touch-action:none;cursor:grab\" transform=\"translate(70,230)\">\n<circle r=\"44\" fill=\"transparent\"/>\n<circle class=\"knobdot\" r=\"14\"/>\n<path d=\"M0 -6 L-5 -1 L5 -1 Z M0 6 L-5 1 L5 1 Z\" fill=\"var(--bench)\"/>\n</g>\n</svg></div><div class=\"side\"><div class=\"readouts\"><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"lenOut-name\">Length L (m)</div><output id=\"lenOut\" data-synapse-readout=\"lenOut\" aria-labelledby=\"lenOut-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"perOut-name\">Period T (s)</div><output id=\"perOut\" data-synapse-readout=\"perOut\" aria-labelledby=\"perOut-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"sqOut-name\">T squared (s2)</div><output id=\"sqOut\" data-synapse-readout=\"sqOut\" aria-labelledby=\"sqOut-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"freqOut-name\">Frequency f (Hz)</div><output id=\"freqOut\" data-synapse-readout=\"freqOut\" aria-labelledby=\"freqOut-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"cntOut-name\">Swings in 20 s</div><output id=\"cntOut\" data-synapse-readout=\"cntOut\" aria-labelledby=\"cntOut-name\"></output></div></div><p id=\"found\" class=\"card found\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p><details class=\"card fine\"><summary>Keyboard controls</summary><div class=\"row\"><label for=\"length\">Pendulum length L</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"length\" data-synapse-control=\"length\" min=\"0.1\" max=\"1\" step=\"0.05\" value=\"0.5\" data-unit=\"m\" aria-valuetext=\"0.5 m\"></div></details></div></section><section class=\"card hints\"><h2>Need a hint?</h2><details><summary>Hint 1</summary><p>The reference pendulum is 0.25 m long and its period is about 1.0 s. Compare your pendulum with it.</p></details><details><summary>Hint 2</summary><p>Try L = 0.25 m and L = 1.00 m. Work out how many times bigger L is and how many times bigger T is.</p></details><details><summary>Hint 3</summary><p>T is proportional to the square root of L. If L is 4 times bigger, T is 2 times bigger. T squared is proportional to L.</p></details></section><section class=\"explain\"><h2>Why it happens</h2><p>A pendulum swings because gravity pulls the bob back towards the lowest point. A longer string makes the bob travel along a longer arc, and the restoring push along that arc is weaker compared with the distance the bob has to go. So each swing takes more time.</p><p>For small swings the period is T = 2 x pi x sqrt(L / g), where g = 9.81 m/s2. The mass of the bob does not appear in the formula, because a heavier bob is pulled harder by gravity but also has more inertia, and the two effects cancel.</p><p>Because T depends on the square root of L, making L 4 times longer only doubles T. T squared is proportional to L, so a graph of T squared against L is a straight line through the origin. This is how a pendulum is used in the lab to measure g.</p></section></main><script>\naddEventListener(\"message\", function (e) {\n  var d = e.data;\n  if (d && typeof d === \"object\" && d.type === \"synapse_theme\" && (d.theme === \"light\" || d.theme === \"dark\")) document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", d.theme);\n});\nArray.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll(\"input[data-synapse-control]\"), function (el) {\n  function say() { el.setAttribute(\"aria-valuetext\", el.value + (el.dataset.unit ? \" \" + el.dataset.unit : \"\")); }\n  el.addEventListener(\"input\", say);\n  say();\n});\n\n(function () {\nvar svg = document.getElementById(\"bench-art\");\nvar NS = svg.namespaceURI;\nvar slider = document.getElementById(\"length\");\nvar G_MS2 = 9.81;\nvar SC_PX = 360;\nvar PY = 50;\nvar MX = 270;\nvar RX = 500;\nvar REF_LEN_M = 0.25;\nvar AMP_RAD = 12 * Math.PI / 180;\nvar STEP_M = 0.05;\nvar MIN_M = 0.1;\nvar MAX_M = 1.0;\n\nfunction periodS(lengthM) { return 2 * Math.PI * Math.sqrt(lengthM / G_MS2); }\n\nvar ticks = document.getElementById(\"ticks\");\nfor (var i = 0; i <= 10; i++) {\n  var ty = PY + i * 0.1 * SC_PX;\n  var ln = document.createElementNS(NS, \"line\");\n  ln.setAttribute(\"class\", \"tk\");\n  ln.setAttribute(\"x1\", i % 5 === 0 ? 60 : 64);\n  ln.setAttribute(\"x2\", 78);\n  ln.setAttribute(\"y1\", ty);\n  ln.setAttribute(\"y2\", ty);\n  ticks.appendChild(ln);\n  if (i % 2 === 0) {\n    var tx = document.createElementNS(NS, \"text\");\n    tx.setAttribute(\"class\", \"mut\");\n    tx.setAttribute(\"x\", 56);\n    tx.setAttribute(\"y\", ty + 4);\n    tx.setAttribute(\"text-anchor\", \"end\");\n    tx.textContent = (i / 10).toFixed(1);\n    ticks.appendChild(tx);\n  }\n}\n\nvar phase = 0;\nvar lengthM = 0.5;\nvar el = {};\n[\"guide\",\"arcM\",\"arcR\",\"strM\",\"bobM\",\"strR\",\"bobR\",\"tM\",\"tR\",\"knob\",\"lenOut\",\"perOut\",\"sqOut\",\"freqOut\",\"cntOut\",\"found\"].forEach(function (k) { el[k] = document.getElementById(k); });\n\nfunction arcPath(cx, r) {\n  var sx = r * Math.sin(AMP_RAD), sy = PY + r * Math.cos(AMP_RAD);\n  return \"M \" + (cx - sx).toFixed(1) + \" \" + sy.toFixed(1) + \" A \" + r.toFixed(1) + \" \" + r.toFixed(1) + \" 0 0 0 \" + (cx + sx).toFixed(1) + \" \" + sy.toFixed(1);\n}\n\nfunction render(theta) {\n  var r = lengthM * SC_PX;\n  var bx = MX + r * Math.sin(theta), by = PY + r * Math.cos(theta);\n  el.strM.setAttribute(\"x2\", bx.toFixed(1));\n  el.strM.setAttribute(\"y2\", by.toFixed(1));\n  el.bobM.setAttribute(\"cx\", bx.toFixed(1));\n  el.bobM.setAttribute(\"cy\", by.toFixed(1));\n  var rr = REF_LEN_M * SC_PX;\n  var rx = RX + rr * Math.sin(theta), ry = PY + rr * Math.cos(theta);\n  el.strR.setAttribute(\"x2\", rx.toFixed(1));\n  el.strR.setAttribute(\"y2\", ry.toFixed(1));\n  el.bobR.setAttribute(\"cx\", rx.toFixed(1));\n  el.bobR.setAttribute(\"cy\", ry.toFixed(1));\n}\n\nfunction update() {\n  lengthM = parseFloat(slider.value);\n  var T = periodS(lengthM);\n  var T2 = T * T;\n  var f = 1 / T;\n  var n = 20 / T;\n  el.lenOut.textContent = lengthM.toFixed(2) + \" m\";\n  el.perOut.textContent = T.toFixed(2) + \" s\";\n  el.sqOut.textContent = T2.toFixed(2) + \" s2\";\n  el.freqOut.textContent = f.toFixed(2) + \" Hz\";\n  el.cntOut.textContent = n.toFixed(1) + \" swings\";\n  var y = PY + lengthM * SC_PX;\n  el.knob.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(70,\" + y.toFixed(1) + \")\");\n  el.guide.setAttribute(\"y1\", y);\n  el.guide.setAttribute(\"y2\", y);\n  el.arcM.setAttribute(\"d\", arcPath(MX, lengthM * SC_PX));\n  el.arcR.setAttribute(\"d\", arcPath(RX, REF_LEN_M * SC_PX));\n  el.tM.textContent = \"T = \" + T.toFixed(2) + \" s\";\n  el.tR.textContent = \"T = \" + periodS(REF_LEN_M).toFixed(2) + \" s\";\n  svg.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", \"Pendulum of length \" + lengthM.toFixed(2) + \" metres with period \" + T.toFixed(2) + \" seconds, beside a 0.25 metre reference pendulum with period \" + periodS(REF_LEN_M).toFixed(2) + \" seconds\");\n  el.found.textContent = \"A pendulum \" + lengthM.toFixed(2) + \" m long takes \" + T.toFixed(2) + \" s for one swing, so T squared is \" + T2.toFixed(2) + \" s2 and it makes \" + n.toFixed(1) + \" swings in 20 s.\";\n  render(AMP_RAD * Math.cos(phase));\n}\n\nslider.addEventListener(\"input\", update);\n\nvar dragging = false;\nfunction svgY(ev) {\n  var pt = svg.createSVGPoint();\n  pt.x = ev.clientX;\n  pt.y = ev.clientY;\n  return pt.matrixTransform(svg.getScreenCTM().inverse()).y;\n}\nfunction setFromPointer(ev) {\n  var L = (svgY(ev) - PY) / SC_PX;\n  L = Math.round(L / STEP_M) * STEP_M;\n  L = Math.max(MIN_M, Math.min(MAX_M, L));\n  slider.value = L.toFixed(2);\n  slider.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"input\", {bubbles: true}));\n}\nel.knob.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", function (ev) {\n  dragging = true;\n  el.knob.setPointerCapture(ev.pointerId);\n  el.knob.style.cursor = \"grabbing\";\n  setFromPointer(ev);\n  ev.preventDefault();\n});\nel.knob.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", function (ev) {\n  if (dragging) setFromPointer(ev);\n});\nfunction endDrag() {\n  dragging = false;\n  el.knob.style.cursor = \"grab\";\n}\nel.knob.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", endDrag);\nel.knob.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", endDrag);\n\nvar reduce = window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\").matches;\nvar lastTs = null;\nfunction frame(ts) {\n  if (lastTs !== null) {\n    var dt = (ts - lastTs) / 1000;\n    if (dt > 0.1) dt = 0.1;\n    phase += dt / periodS(lengthM) * 2 * Math.PI;\n  }\n  lastTs = ts;\n  render(AMP_RAD * Math.cos(phase));\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\nupdate();\nif (!reduce) requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n})();</script></body></html>","citations":[{"source":"UNVERIFIED (no textbook page has been checked for this Environment)","page":null,"quote":null,"verified":false,"printedPage":null}],"checked":{"layers":["postprocess","scan","render","wording"],"controlsExercised":1,"gridPoints":0,"referenceCases":0,"readouts":5,"models":[],"limits":"Written whole by a model and not built on the Kit, so none of its numbers or formulas were compared with an audited science model. Code checked that it runs and that its controls work and a second model read its words and formulas, but only for a short, scripted stretch of time. No textbook source was checked and a person has not reviewed it. Check it against your textbook."},"planSummary":"A page written whole by a model for a question the Kit could not express (topic physics_form4_waves)."}